      "instructions": "Percher publishes web apps to <name>.percher.run.\nCanonical flow: percher_publish -> percher_wait_for_deploy -> if recovery.nextAction='run_doctor': percher_doctor -> follow its recovery until 'none' or 'ask_user'.\nEvery tool that can fail returns a machine-readable `recovery` field. Always read recovery.nextAction; never regex-parse the human text.\nCall EXACTLY the suggested tool with EXACTLY recovery.args \u2014 fields like mode and deployId are load-bearing.\nIf nextAction='ask_user', ask recovery.prompt verbatim and wait.\npercher_publish defaults to async (returns 'queued' fast); pass waitForLive:true only if the user wants to block.\nNo token? publish returns auth_pending with a login URL; follow recovery (wait_auth). Check recovery.alternativeActions for the anonymous-publish path.\npercher_doctor is the recovery hub for any unclear failure."
